# SPA rewrites for the app's client routes ONLY (see src/app.tsx). Everything
# else that misses a static file gets public/404.html with a real 404 status.
#
# This is deliberate and load-bearing: a catch-all /* rewrite used to answer
# missing /assets/* chunk URLs with index.html as HTTP 200. During a deploy's
# edge-propagation window that let browsers (and the service worker's install
# precache) cache HTML bodies under hashed .js/.css URLs — poisoning clients
# so the app could never boot again (2026-08-05 incident). A 404 can never be
# cached as a module, and a failed service worker install cleanly retries.
/project/*    /index.html   200
/unlocked     /index.html   200
/about        /index.html   200
/privacy      /index.html   200
/terms        /index.html   200
